.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
For functions that return signed integers, a 0 indicates that the function exited successfully.
If instead a negative number is returned, it indicates a specific error that occurred during function's execution.
The returned error codes are made to resemble POSIX in both meaning and numeric value.
.PP
The lifetime of most object is tied to the parent \fIhidpp_receiver_t\fR object,
Exceptions to this are input handlers from \fIhidpp_input_open\fR and
\fIhidpp_receiver_info\fR structures, which are freed by the \fIhidpp_free_info\fR function.
